OpenPyCharm Database

The dev.openpycharm.database implementation is independent source authored for
OpenPyCharm, licensed under this repository's Apache License 2.0. It uses public
open-source IntelliJ Platform APIs, native IntelliJ editors/Swing and JDBC.
No proprietary PyCharm Database Tools implementation, assets or source are used.

Unmodified driver JARs are separate, replaceable files under lib. Exact versions,
upstream links, SHA-256 hashes and Maven Central URLs are in drivers.lock.json:

- Xerial SQLite JDBC 3.54.1.0: Apache License 2.0; the original Zentus driver
  notice uses the BSD license. SQLite itself is in the public domain. The
  original driver license files remain in the JAR and are reproduced in legal.
- PostgreSQL JDBC 42.7.13: BSD 2-Clause. Bundled SCRAM/stringprep component
  notices remain in its unmodified JAR and are reproduced in legal.
- MariaDB Connector/J 3.5.11: LGPL 2.1 or later, copyright MariaDB and contributors.
  This driver supports MariaDB and MySQL protocol servers. The exact matching,
  unmodified source JAR is distributed under legal next to LGPL/GPL license
  texts. Users may replace the separate driver JAR with a compatible modified
  version and reverse engineer/debug those library modifications as permitted
  by the LGPL. OpenPyCharm imposes no additional restriction on those rights.

The driver downloads are explicitly provisioned and hash authenticated before
offline compilation/packaging. No production or other user database is accessed
by the integration checks; those use an owned temporary SQLite file.
